// mn-multishot — STEP 3 gate: the MULTI-SHOT PRODUCER.
//
// A handler arm with TWO sequential (non-disjoint) resume sites classifies
// MultiShot (infer_resume_cardinality: multiple sites, not branch-disjoint).
// The continuation must be reified (LMakeContinuation) and CALLED TWICE — the
// arm resumes once with 10, once with 20; the body after `pick()` doubles its
// input and the handler sums the two runs: (1*10) + (1*20) = 30, NOT the
// one-shot 10. Proves the producer mints the heap record and the catching
// handler re-enters it a second time.
//
// LAW 7: the OneShot path (every ev*/eq micro) stays byte-identical — this is
// an ADDED form, not a perturbation. The MultiShot producer fires ONLY for an
// arm the body proves multi-shot.
//
// Run: tools/run-micro.sh tests/micros/mn-multishot.mn 30
// Expected exit 30: total = run(10) + run(20) = 10 + 20.

effect Pick { pick() -> Int }

// Two resume sites, sequential in the arm body → MultiShot. Each resume runs
// the continuation (the rest of `body`, which returns its input) and the arm
// sums the two resumptions' results.
handler twice with total = 0 {
  pick() => {
    let a = resume(10)
    let b = resume(20)
    a + b
  }
}

fn body() = pick()

fn main(q) = { body() } ~> twice
